            "text": "cross stitch crochet"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " throw is 90 x 100 cm. Each pair of trebles is worked out of order: the second stitch first, then the first stitch in front of it. The crossing produces an X on the surface."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "In aran weight the X shapes are prominent and make the fabric look woven. The cross pairs draw in slightly, making the fabric narrower than a regular treble row of the same stitch count. Total yardage is around 700 g."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "What you need"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "suppliesCard",
        "attrs": {
          "heading": "Materials",
          "items": [
            {
              "name": "Aran yarn",
              "qty": "700 g"
            },
            {
              "name": "5 mm crochet hook",
              "qty": "1"
            },
            {
              "name": "Tapestry needle",
              "qty": "1"
            },
            {
              "name": "Scissors",
              "qty": "1 pair"
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "How to work a cross pair"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Skip 1 stitch. Work 1 tr into the next stitch (2nd stitch). Work 1 tr into the skipped stitch, bringing the hook in front of the first treble. One cross pair made (2 stitches used)."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Gauge"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "12 cross pairs x 7 rows = 10 x 10 cm in aran with a 5 mm hook. One cross pair uses 2 stitches. Foundation chain must be an even number."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Stitches used"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "bulletList",
        "content": [
          {
